  "articleBody": "It's a common scenario: you fall in love with a new bathroom vanity, bring it home, and then realize it doesn't quite fit. There are a few reasons this happens, and knowing them can help you avoid the frustration. Often, folks forget to precisely measure the available width in their bathroom. Even an inch can make a big difference, especially in smaller spaces. Another key issue is the plumbing rough-in. Your new vanity might have different dimensions or sink configurations that don't align with your existing water supply and drain lines. This doesn't mean it won't work, but it does mean plumbing adjustments will be needed, which adds to the scope of work. Also, if your bathroom walls or floor aren't perfectly even, a new, precisely built vanity might highlight those imperfections, making it hard to level and install properly. This is especially true with custom-fabricated or stone tops. These aren't insurmountable problems, but they do mean you might need professional help to get that seamless, perfect fit. For help with your bathroom vanity installation, including custom fits and plumbing adjustments, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
